g 3:** the bill requires notice whether or not parents ask.\n- **Why rung 4 and not rung 5:** the committee draft required a parent's written permission before staff used a different name or pronoun, and the final law drops that.\n- **Earlier vote:** her February third-reading Yea (Roll Call 220) and the committee draft are coded `superseded-by-later` and `direction-only`. I don't have the exact text she voted on at third reading, so I listed it in `needs_source`.\n- **Judgement call:** the bill also bans sexuality instruction for pre-K through grade 3. I treated that as a related school provision rather than a multi-subject omnibus. If reviewers read the bill as multi-subject, a Yea on final passage shows only a side, and the row would become BLANK `direction-only`.\n\nThere are no quotes, because none of the sources contain her own words.\n\nSeparately, several connectors (Benevity, Candid, Canva, Figma, Givebutter, Harvey, WorkOS) need authorizing in your claude.ai connector settings, and the GitHub plugin failed to connect. None of them were needed for this task.","ttft_ms":43328,"type":"result","duration_ms":66474,"uuid":"58cc53c7-8619-4824-b15d-a84929d5f408","ttft_stream_ms":19900,"time_to_request_ms":309,"first_content_frame_ms":19900,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
